---
// Homepage teaser for /substrate. Static (the homepage stays prerendered); the
// live world lives on its own page.
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
  <a href="/substrate" class="group block" data-section-reveal>
    <div
      class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border p-8 transition-colors md:p-12"
      style="border-color: var(--color-border); background: radial-gradient(120% 100% at 20% 0%, rgba(122,242,160,0.05), transparent 55%), rgba(255,255,255,0.012);"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest" style="color: var(--color-text-subtle);">
        <span>
          <span class="live-dot mr-2 inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full align-middle" style="background: var(--color-accent);"></span>
          Live
        </span>
        <span style="text-transform: none; letter-spacing: normal;">a shared world, running right now</span>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-5 max-w-3xl text-2xl font-medium md:text-4xl" style="color: var(--color-text); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Watch an AI platform live and breathe.
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">
        An orchestrator routes work to a crew of agents. Retrievers query a memory core, an eval
        judge scores every output, and a supervisor quarantines the ones that fail. It's the stack
        I build, rendered as an organism you can poke.
      </p>

      <span class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm transition-colors group-hover:[color:var(--color-accent)]" style="color: var(--color-text);">
        Enter the Substrate
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5">→</span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </a>
</section>
